    "result_text": "The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain blocklist so that creating (or updating) an owner with an email on the blocklist returns **400**.\n\nThe email is normalized centrally in `OwnerEmail.normalize`, which both the create pipeline (`ValidateNewOwner`) and the update pipeline (`ValidateOwner`) call \u2014 so the single change covers both endpoints. Following the repo's escalation conventions:\n\n- **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 after syntactic validation and lower-casing, extracts the domain and rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` (case-insensitive, via the already-lowercased value) by throwing a new checked `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in `throws` clauses.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`.\n- **`officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- Added the exception to the `throws` clauses of `ValidateNewOwner` and `ValidateOwner`.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
